# Team memory for kube-noob

Each file in `entries/` records one thing your team learned about a Kubernetes or OpenShift problem: the signals it
shows (alert names, event and container reasons, error templates), the symptom, the cause, the fix, references to the
evidence, and what happened each time someone applied it. kube-noob shows approved entries next to its playbooks and
known issues, cited as `[mem:MEM-<n>]`.

This repository belongs to your team. kube-noob reads it where it runs (CLI, MCP server, in-cluster sidecar) and never
uploads, bundles, publishes or exports it as training data.

## Add an entry

```bash
kube-noob memory add . --symptom "etcd leader changes every few minutes after the update" --cause "catalog sync I/O on the control-plane disks" --fix "update to the release that fixes it; lower catalog polling until then" --signal alert:etcdHighNumberOfLeaderChanges --platform openshift --owner platform-team
kube-noob memory validate .
```

`add` writes `entries/MEM-<n>.yaml` with `status: proposed` and never commits. Review it in a pull request; a reviewer
sets `status: approved` when the fix is confirmed. Set `status: retired` when it no longer applies.

## What an entry may hold

- Summaries in words. Credentials, raw logs, event rows, stack traces, command pipelines and manifests in prose are
  rejected.
- Commands, one per line, labelled `read-only` or `needs-approval` exactly as kube-noob's classifier labels them. A
  command never prints a Secret.
- A `patch`: complete manifests that `oc apply` accepts. Never a Secret.
- Evidence as references only: an https URL, a ticket key, a `kn:` or `mem:` citation, or `bundle:<dir>/<file>`.
- Versions in quotes (`fixedIn: "4.20"`): unquoted, 4.20 reads as the number 4.2.

`entry.schema.json` describes the shape for editors (YAML language servers). `kube-noob memory validate` checks the
content as well, and runs every fix through the verifier: patches are validated, audited and red-teamed, and grants of
the privileged SCC, cluster-admin, hostPath or wildcard RBAC fail unless the entry records `riskAccepted` with an
owner and a reason.

## Record what happened

```bash
kube-noob memory outcome . MEM-12 --result resolved --ticket INC-4211 --cluster prod-east
kube-noob memory stats . --by cluster
```

## Find entries for an error

```bash
kube-noob memory match "etcd leader changed frequently after the update" --dir . --version 4.21.2
kube-noob memory match -f alert.json --dir .
```

Generated by kube-noob $version (`kube-noob memory init`). CI: `.github/workflows/kube-noob-memory.yml` or
`scripts/validate-memory.sh`.
